# Performance Guidelines

## Angular Frontend

### Change Detection – Always OnPush

Every component must declare `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`. Signals + OnPush = zero wasted re-renders:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
@Component({
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
  ...
})

// ❌ WRONG – default strategy re-renders on every event
@Component({ /* no changeDetection */ })
```

### @for – Track by stable identity

Never use `track $index` unless items truly have no stable key:

```html
<!-- ✅ Stable track key -->
@for (v of versions(); track v.version) { ... }

<!-- ❌ Forces full DOM rebuild on any array change -->
@for (v of versions(); track $index) { ... }
```

### No Function Calls in Templates

Function calls run on every change-detection cycle. Use `computed()` or pipes instead:

```typescript
// ❌ Recalculates every cycle
{{ formatLabel(v.version) }}

// ✅ Computed only when dependency changes
readonly versionLabel = computed(() => formatLabel(this.version()));
```

### Lazy Loading

All routes beyond the root shell must use `loadComponent()`:

```typescript
// ✅
{ path: 'settings', loadComponent: () => import('./settings/settings.component').then(m => m.SettingsComponent) }

// ❌
{ path: 'settings', component: SettingsComponent }
```

### rxResource() for HTTP Resources

Prefer `rxResource()` over manual `ngOnInit` + subscribe for data that maps 1:1 to an HTTP call:

```typescript
readonly versions = rxResource({
  loader: () => this.nvmApi.getInstalledVersions()
});
// versions.value() / versions.isLoading() / versions.error() available as signals
```

---

## Node.js Backend

### Never Block the Event Loop

```typescript
// ❌ Blocks the event loop
const data = fs.readFileSync(path);

// ✅ Non-blocking
const data = await fs.promises.readFile(path);
```

All I/O inside request handlers: `fs.promises.*`, `execFileAsync` (promisified), never synchronous variants.

### execFile – Not exec

`execFile` avoids spawning a shell for the outer command, reducing overhead and attack surface:

```typescript
// ✅ execFile – no extra shell
import { execFile } from 'node:child_process';
execFile('bash', ['-c', nvmCommand], options, callback);

// ❌ exec – spawns shell twice
import { exec } from 'node:child_process';
exec(nvmCommand, callback);
```

### MaxBuffer for ls-remote

`nvm ls-remote --lts` outputs ~500 KB. Set `maxBuffer` accordingly:

```typescript
const options = { maxBuffer: 10 * 1024 * 1024 }; // 10 MB
```

### Timeout for Long Operations

Install/uninstall can take minutes. Default `execFile` timeout (undefined = infinite) is too permissive:

```typescript
const options = { timeout: 180_000 }; // 3 minutes
```
